<item>
            <title>[PARQUET-172] Add support for non-String binary in parquet-thrift</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-172</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Thrift &lt;a href=&quot;https://thrift.apache.org/docs/types&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;considers binary a &quot;special&quot; type&lt;/a&gt; that isn&apos;t in the official spec but is &quot;to provide better interoperability with java&quot;. The parquet-thrift side doesn&apos;t currently support binary because Thrift String fields are converted to UTF8-annotated binary. The result is that binary fields get mangled when stored in Parquet because Parquet assumes they are UTF8.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I think some storage layer in Java Thrift must know about binary and pass the unencoded bytes, but that Parquet hasn&apos;t implemented a similar hack. (The &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-parquet-mr/blob/master/parquet-thrift/src/main/java/parquet/thrift/ThriftSchemaConverter.java#L86&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;type conversion&lt;/a&gt; code at least has no entry for binary.)&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12770545">PARQUET-172</key>
            <summary>Add support for non-String binary in parquet-thrift</summary>
                <type id="1" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/viewavatar?size=xsmall&amp;avatarId=21133&amp;avatarType=issuetype">Bug</type>
