                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="14355894" author="rdblue" created="Tue, 10 Mar 2015 23:01:59 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This was based on a &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/laurencer/parquet-mr-bug/commit/d09126e03e2dc9f60eb5fd7b13b8166ab4d52ba0&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;reported parquet-scrooge bug&lt;/a&gt; and an incomplete analysis on my part. I looked only at the Schema converter, which doesn&apos;t show support for binary but doesn&apos;t need it. Support for binary already exists; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-parquet-mr/blob/master/parquet-thrift/src/main/java/parquet/thrift/ParquetWriteProtocol.java#L298&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;&lt;tt&gt;ParquetWriteProtocol&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/a&gt; allows binary data to be written as either a String or binar, and the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-parquet-mr/blob/master/parquet-thrift/src/main/java/parquet/thrift/ThriftRecordConverter.java#L413&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;&lt;tt&gt;ThriftRecordConverter&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/a&gt; generates correct protocol events that handle both.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It turns out that the original bug report wasn&apos;t correct. The summary does appear to have corrupt data:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;Parquet Example
---------------

    ./sbt &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;run-main com.rouesnel.parquetmr.bug.ParquetExample&quot;&lt;/span&gt;

This should print the following:

    Parquet
    =======

    Parquet File written to /some/random/location/test-324324-foo.parquet

    After encoding - binary field is equal to original binary field: &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;
    After encoding - binary field is equal to UTF8 encoded binary field: &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;


    Original
    -----
    binaryField:         -123, 20, 33
    stringField:         foo
    binaryAsStringField: -17, -65, -67, 20, 33



    Thrift Serialized
    -----
    binaryField:         3, 0, 0, 0, -123, 20, 33
    stringField:         foo
    binaryAsStringField: -17, -65, -67, 20, 33
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tests show that the underlying byte buffers are correct and the error is caused by assuming the ByteBuffer&apos;s backing array contains only the bytes serialized. When restricted to the position and limit, the data is correct.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14355914" author="rdblue" created="Tue, 10 Mar 2015 23:16:17 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Added tests to validate binary support in &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-parquet-mr/pull/145&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;PR #145&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17857135" author="rok" created="Sun, 23 Jun 2024 03:27:09 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This issue has been migrated to &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/parquet-java/issues/1722&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;issue #1722&lt;/a&gt; on GitHub. Please see the &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-2502&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;migration documentation&lt;/a&gt; for further details.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
